Statement of changes (Apache-2.0 section 4b)
--------------------------------------------
KapAble modifies the original Dyad source as follows:

* Renamed the product and its identifiers, user-facing copy, localizations,
  URL scheme, on-disk paths and response tags from Dyad to KapAble.
* Removed the bundled product-analytics project key. No analytics are
  collected unless an operator supplies their own key at build time.
* Replaced hard-coded hosted-service endpoints with configuration that is
  unset by default, so features depending on services operated by Dyad Tech,
  Inc. are disabled rather than directed at those services.
* Disabled the software update feed by default.
* Repointed in-application help links to this project's own documentation.

The following upstream identifiers are retained deliberately, because they
refer to artifacts published and operated by the Dyad project rather than to
KapAble: the "@dyad-sh" npm package scope, the "data-dyad-*" DOM attributes
emitted by the Dyad component tagger, and the "dyad-sh" GitHub organization's
starter template repositories.

